{"parentUuid":"fe539c9b-1f26-41d8-9e52-581581cc8d04","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"qwen3.7-plus","id":"msg_0b1feccd-7786-4491-a9b3-0a595d650e3c","role":"assistant","type":"message","content":[{"type":"thinking","signature":"","thinking":"The user wants me to diagnose why all 14 stocks failed in the \"持仓池体检\" (step 5) of the pre_market_pipeline.py. I've now read both `pre_market_pipeline.py` and `stock_diagoser.py`. \n\nThe key is in the `diagnose()` function (line 1615 of stock_diagoser.py):\n\n```python\ndef diagnose(code: str, pool_meta: dict | None = None) -> dict:\n    code = dl._clean_code(code)\n    ...\n    snap = dl.get_stock_realtime(code)\n\n\n```\n\nAnd in `collect_watchlist()` (line 240 of pre_market_pipeline.py):\n\n```python\ndef collect_watchlist() -> dict:\n    pool = _load_pool()\n    ...\n    for item in pool:\n        code = item.get(\"ticker\", \"\")\n        if not code:\n            continue\n        try:\n            r = stock_diagoser.diagnose(code, pool_meta=item)\n            results.append(r)\n        except Exception as e:\n            results.append({\"ok\": False, \"code\": code, \"name\": item.\n```\n\nI can see that the diagnose function fetches real-time stock data and historical data, then checks if both calls failed. The collect_watchlist function wraps each diagnosis call in a try-except block, catching any exceptions and marking them as failed results. So the issue is likely that either the data layer functions are throwing exceptions or returning failures for all 14 stocks.\n\nLooking at the output, all 14 stocks show empty names and prices with the failure marker, which suggests the exception path is being triggered for each one. The error details aren't being displayed in the output, so I need to check how the markdown renderer is handling these failed results to understand what's actually happening. The issue is likely that all 14 stocks are throwing exceptions in the diagnose function, and the error handling is catching them but rendering them as empty rows. I need to trace through three things: what the `data_layer.py` functions are doing that might fail across all stocks, how `md_renderer.py` actually displays the watchlist results, and whether the exception is being silently caught and formatted as empty cells in the table.\n"}],"usage":{"input_tokens":47893,"output_tokens":0}},"attributionSkill":"claude-stock","type":"assistant","uuid":"a5f0336c-4f0c-4bb3-bf48-67aa4c13f5e6","timestamp":"2026-08-14T01:22:45.015Z","effort":"high","session_id":"df33713e-6c00-4d1f-af2a-9d28a323194c","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"E:\\playgroud","sessionId":"df33713e-6c00-4d1f-af2a-9d28a323194c","version":"2.1.229","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"concurrent-brewing-kay"}
